A||N||7||Jay||Anyone ever import a Fiero into the US?||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||12-02-2001||03:49 PM||||As many may know I sold the N* last night on ebay.  The new owner will pick the car up in Windsor Ontario (across the boarder from Detroit).  I'm having a hard time (and so is he) figuring out what is required to import a car into the US.  I have the compliance letter from GM stating the vehicle meets all DOT and EPA specs and is legal for import, but what does he have to do on his end?  Anyone ever done this?<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||lou||12-02-2001||05:38 PM||||Jay you are going to have to drive it over the border for him in order to avoid a customs problem he may encounter.  He can then drive it home from there and deal with the dmv in his state. email me for more details.||||reg||1
Z||000002||newfie||12-02-2001||08:31 PM||||I don't know about CAN-&gt;US, but I was looking into importing from the US-&gt; CAN.  Apperently if the car is 15 years old, as I believe yours is it is really easy.  I got my info mostly from <A HREF="http://www.riv.ca" TARGET=_blank>www.riv.ca</A>   This is for importing to Canada, maybe they have some info for going the other way. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||12-03-2001||03:26 AM||||Varies royally from state-state, BUT if you just show up at the DMV, and don't leave untill you have it registered, that'll probally work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (Unless he lives in the People's Republic of California...)<P>You will need to drive it into the country for him.  <P>Enjoy the Ferrari man, you lucky dog!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Jay||12-03-2001||10:15 AM||||He does live in California but he is meeting me in Windsor/Detroit.  What's the difference with Cali?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||12-03-2001||01:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>He does live in California but he is meeting me in Windsor/Detroit</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bummer.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  For a minute I thought that the Detroit area might be getting another V8...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||thomas_l||12-03-2001||01:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>He does live in California but he is meeting me in Windsor/Detroit.  What's the difference with Cali?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Artherd's "People's Republic" remark is the short version. Aside from a brutal emissions program Cali has one of the worst beaurocracies in the US for any type of State business. In fact they set the standard for the other 49 states. If you've ever heard "BAR 84" or "BAR 90" mingled in a discussion about emission testing that would be the California Bureau of Automotive Repair. In fact that whole tree-hugging emissions thing is the reason it takes me 45 minutes to drive 6 miles to work in the morning. Metro Atlanta failed the EPA highway funding for 3 years in a row and the major thru route near my house is the only 2 lane (gridlock) section in two counties  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">. The feds withheld highway funds which delayed the last widening project. In their infinite government wisdom they have "improved" our air quality by blocking a road project and keeping traffic standing still.<P>If I went into a Georgia tag/title office they would probably not notice that Ontario is not one of the 50 states much less be able to spell it.||||reg||8
Z||000007||terryk||12-03-2001||03:10 PM||||Well, the California emissions standards aren't that bad but the air here was pure poison for many years. I know many of us don't give it a second thought, but the emissions standards have helped. The problem is when you are marginal, dealing with it really sucks.<P>And before we start with the fruits and nuts jokes, remember: Our agricultural inspection stations are for the incoming, not outgoing. Feel free to take all of your fruits and nuts with you.||||reg||6
